// Syncthing ignore list, linked into each shared folder as .stignore.
//
// The shared folders are deliberately narrow: Claude's projects/ and Codex's
// sessions/. Both hold append-only JSONL, one file per session id, so two
// machines writing at the same time touch different files and no merge is ever
// needed. That is what makes these safe to sync live, unlike a browser profile
// or Codex's thread_history/logs/queue SQLite stores, which are excluded by
// simply not sharing the directories they live in.

// macOS turds.
.DS_Store
._*

// Defensive: if a database ever appears inside one of these folders, do not
// replicate it. Syncthing copies files, not transactions, so a live SQLite
// file synced mid-write arrives corrupt.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

// Editor and tooling scratch.
*.tmp
*.swp
